WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.888
In the twenty-fourth year of Jian'an, Guan Yu led his great army to attack Xiangfan; banners flew, and his might shook all China.

00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:10.406
When enemy troops everywhere heard his name, they all felt afraid.

00:00:10.756 --> 00:00:16.108
Unexpectedly, Sun Quan broke the alliance and sent troops to sneak-attack Jingzhou; Guan Yu was suddenly attacked from front and back.

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:19.986
When news came that Jingzhou had fallen, the army's morale began to waver.

00:00:20.336 --> 00:00:25.784
Guan Yu's soldiers slipped away one by one, until only a few men remained following him.

00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:30.094
Those who stayed followed him closely, not leaving by a single step.

00:00:30.444 --> 00:00:35.244
In the pouring rain, Guan Yu led his remaining troops in a difficult retreat to Maicheng.

00:00:35.594 --> 00:00:39.434
The rain soaked their clothes; the mountain road was muddy and hard to walk.

00:00:39.784 --> 00:00:44.896
The Wu army surrounded Maicheng layer upon layer; captured, Guan Yu still stood tall with head held high, preferring death to surrender.

00:00:45.246 --> 00:00:48.966
His gaze was firm, and he faced the end of his life with calm dignity.

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:55.676
As the sun set in the west, a great general's curtain fell; his loyalty and honor are remembered forever.

00:00:56.026 --> 00:00:59.098
Later generations built temples to honor this loyal and righteous hero.

